+      phi_n(c_sigma 3^(1/4) [z + eta^(1/3)]),
+  c_R = 1, c_I = -i,
+  phi_n(w) = pi^(-1/4) (2^n n!)^(-1/2) exp(-w^2/2) H_n(w).
+
+Conventions are eta=|F|/V>0, delta=hbar*omega_0/V,
+z=eta^(1/3)y, epsilon=eta^(-2/3), and
