+The local formula excludes z=0, has only local normalization, and is
+controlled only in a close-turning-point neighbourhood on an appropriate
+sector.  It is not proved to be a global Bargmann eigenfunction.  Iteration
+repeatedly uses it outside that neighbourhood and has no asserted physical
+time-evolution meaning.  The output is therefore an exploratory numerical
+portrait, not a spectral or dynamical result.
