+BRANCHES AND REGULARIZATION
+---------------------------
+NumPy principal branches are used for log and complex powers.  No Riemann
+sheets, analytic-continuation tracking, branch-cut masks, or Stokes-aware
+continuation are constructed.  Principal-branch discontinuities are allowed
+to remain visible and must not be read as physical singularities or evidence
+of fractality.
+
+The exact naive regularization policy is:
+
+1. Every complex denominator d with |d|<eps_den is replaced by
+   eps_den exp(i arg(d)); d=0 receives phase zero.
+2. Before exponentiation, only the real part of an exponent is clipped to
+   [-exp_clip,+exp_clip]; its imaginary part is retained.
+3. After each map application, non-finite values are marked invalid and
+   replaced internally by a sentinel zero; invalidity propagates.
+4. Remaining finite values with modulus above z_cap are capped radially to
+   z_cap with phase preserved.
+5. Invalid pixels are black.  No smoothing, interpolation, or manufactured
+   post-processing is used.
